WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.334 line:0%
-Sir, Paul Rudd wants you
to see "Bros."

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:03.136 line:0%
-What's up, Paul Rudd?

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:04.170 line:0%
-You guys gonna see "Bros"?

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.705 line:0%
My new movie, September 30th.

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.206 line:0%
-I'm one of the Bros
so I got to watch.

00:00:07.206 --> 00:00:08.607 line:0%
-Tell all your bros
to see "Bros."

00:00:08.674 --> 00:00:10.042 line:0%
-Tell all your bros
to see "Bros."

00:00:10.042 --> 00:00:12.212 line:0%
-Come on, man. Yeah. [Bleep].

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:15.314
Yeah.
-A lot of gay sex in it.

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:17.116
-Whoa.
-Oh, okay.

00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:18.951
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.951 --> 00:00:20.119
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:21.988
We're here with Billy Eichner.

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:26.059
It's been
a while since you've been

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:28.027
back out doing
"Billy on the Street."

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:29.329
-We just released that video.

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:32.164
It's the first "Billy on
the Street" in three years.

00:00:32.164 --> 00:00:34.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:35.668
If you haven't seen it,

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:38.237
it's all over my YouTube
and social media.

00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:41.207
Check it out. Paul Rudd was kind
enough to come and do it.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:43.109
He's done it before.
He's amazing at it.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:46.211
He's fearless.
And it was really fun.

00:00:46.211 --> 00:00:48.481
And it's -- You know, for years
I've been running around

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:51.451
shouting about actors and movie
stars and their movies.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.686
This is the first time I get to
shout about my own movie.

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:55.587
-Yeah, there you go.
It's about time.

00:00:55.587 --> 00:00:58.023
[ Cheers and applause ]
You got to shoot the film in

00:00:58.023 --> 00:01:01.094
New York, and obviously having
done "Billy on the Street"

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:02.762
with you as well,
that's a lot of running

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.797
through the streets of New York.
It is not a controlled set.

00:01:04.797 --> 00:01:07.266
It's very catch as catch can.
-You've done it, yeah.

00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:10.236
-Was it nice to, one, shoot in
a city you're comfortable with

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:13.005
and, two, sort of on controlled
sets where you --

00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:15.307
-Yes, I love "Billy on the
Street," but it's nice to also

00:01:15.307 --> 00:01:18.043
work with actors who've had,
like, scripted lines to say.

00:01:18.043 --> 00:01:19.679
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.313
-But yeah, I mean,
it was written --

00:01:21.313 --> 00:01:24.017
not to get too sentimental about
it, but, you know, I grew up

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:26.886
loving those romantic comedies,
you know, that I mentioned like

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:28.187
"When Harry Met Sally"
and all of those movies.

00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:30.222
And it always, you know,
features like, you know,

00:01:30.222 --> 00:01:33.626
a couple walking around Central
Park and making witty banter.

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:35.661
And me and Luke were doing that
and shooting here

00:01:35.661 --> 00:01:38.197
on the Upper West Side,
and I did take a moment to think

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:41.033
to myself, you know, "Wow, this
is amazing, I'm doing one of

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:44.704
those movies that I love,
but it's about someone like me."

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:47.173
It's about a gay male couple
at the center of it.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.574
And it's real and it's honest.

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:52.177
And it's funny I hope, and that,
I'm very grateful for that.

00:01:52.177 --> 00:01:54.180
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Amazing.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.349
Another thing I'm assuming --

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:58.051
-And let me just say
one more thing.

00:01:58.051 --> 00:01:59.719
-Please.
-Because people -- you know,

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:02.288
people don't respect
romantic comedies, right?

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:05.425
And those are the movies
that I love, you know?

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:07.093
And they're not taken seriously.

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:09.829
But the truth is,
you know, I'm a gay man.

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.731
"Brokeback Mountain"
is a great movie.

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:12.798
I've seen it once.

00:02:12.798 --> 00:02:15.200
"Pretty Woman"
I've seen 50 times.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.669
[ Laughter ]
So let's support

00:02:17.669 --> 00:02:19.872
romantic comedies because we
secretly all love them.

00:02:19.872 --> 00:02:21.407
-Well, you know what
I will tell you?

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:24.076
[ Cheers and applause ]
Every time I'm on a plane

00:02:24.076 --> 00:02:26.078
and I choose the movie that
everybody is --

00:02:26.078 --> 00:02:28.113
the important movie everybody
has told me I had to see.

00:02:28.113 --> 00:02:30.750
If someone in a row ahead is
watching a romantic comedy,

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.618
I realize I just watch
that without sound.

00:02:32.618 --> 00:02:33.852
-Yes. Right, yeah, yeah.

00:02:33.852 --> 00:02:35.621
-Because your eyes are like,
"I remember that."

00:02:35.621 --> 00:02:38.057
-Yeah, exactly.
You're watching

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:40.593
"My Best Friend's Wedding"
through like a small little --

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.461
like between seats.
-And I'm like,

00:02:42.461 --> 00:02:43.863
"Why am I fighting it?

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:46.532
Why am I not just getting it
on my screen?"

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:48.033
This is pretty cool.

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:50.736
Mariah Carey hosted one of your
first screenings of the film.

00:02:50.736 --> 00:02:53.339
-Yes, she did. Not only that.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:56.342
On her own volition she had
a "Bros" dress made

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.777
with the logo of "Bros."

00:02:58.777 --> 00:03:01.514
Mariah has a song in the movie.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:04.083
-Which, again, amazing.
-Yeah, it's incredible.

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:06.518
I had to get in touch with her
to get permission to use it.

00:03:06.518 --> 00:03:08.654
It's in the scene where
my love interest and I meet.

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:10.489
And Mariah comes up a few times

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:11.991
during the movie
because of that.

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:14.327
And then she said "no"
and we sent her the movie

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:18.063
and she loved it and she hosted
a screening and made this dress.

00:03:18.063 --> 00:03:22.768
I mean, I literally, no joke, in
like -- what was it, 1992, 1993,

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:25.238
had my first kiss with a girl,

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:26.839
which shows you
how long ago it was.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:29.074
[ Laughter ]
But I had my first kiss

00:03:29.074 --> 00:03:32.145
with a girl listening to
a Mariah Carey song.

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:34.447
-Well, there you go.
Full circle.

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:36.849
Some pretty fun cameos at
the end of the film.

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:39.018
-There sure are, Seth.
Who you talking about?

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:41.020
-Well, I don't know.
-Yeah.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.855
-It's just cool.
It's just like a cool thing

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:45.291
to stick around till the end.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:47.160
Don't want to give anything
away.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.195
-Yeah, just might be kind of
cool to watch.

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:50.629
-Yeah, exactly, yes.

00:03:50.629 --> 00:03:54.233
Some of your favorite
"Late Night" stars from NBC

00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:55.267
might be featured at
the end of the movie.

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:57.169
-Yeah, maybe.
Might, I don't know.

00:03:57.169 --> 00:03:58.537
-Who knows?
-Just go.

00:03:58.537 --> 00:04:01.074
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:04.844
-So, like all rom-coms, there
are sex scenes in this film.

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:07.680
And I am wondering if that
inspired you to get in, what --

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.715
let's be honest --
you're in fantastic shape.

00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:11.417
-Well, thank you for that.
-Yes.

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:14.754
-I did my best, but it's because
I had to be on screen.

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:16.589
You saw Luke Macfarlane.
-Yeah.

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:19.858
-He's like the best-looking
person anyone has ever seen.

00:04:19.858 --> 00:04:24.263
-He also looks like a person
who has never been in bad shape.

00:04:24.263 --> 00:04:25.898
-Right.
-Yeah.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.799
-He's always looked like
Superman.

00:04:27.799 --> 00:04:30.135
He's like gay Superman,
you know.

00:04:30.135 --> 00:04:32.271
I mean, Superman himself was
pretty gay.

00:04:32.271 --> 00:04:34.740
[ Laughter ]
He was definitely bi.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:36.542
-Yeah.
-He was definitely bi.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:38.878
But no, you know,
it's interesting

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:40.546
'cause I wrote it with Nick.

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:43.082
You know, I just kept thinking,
yeah, we're two guys

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:47.486
but Judd Apatow movies have a
history of hilarious sex scenes

00:04:47.486 --> 00:04:50.322
and physical comedy
and, you know, "Trainwreck" --

00:04:50.322 --> 00:04:53.226
and when Kristen Wiig
and Jon Hamm

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:54.927
are together at the beginning of
"Bridesmaids."

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:56.963
And I thought, "Well, why can't
we do that, too?

00:04:56.963 --> 00:04:58.197
Just because we're two guys.

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:00.933
We're just doing it for laughs
to be funny."

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:02.868
But you never think
while writing it,

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:04.737
"Oh, I'm going to have to do
that."

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:06.305
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:08.808
-I swear you just think,
"What's the funniest thing

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:10.276
that could happen
for these characters?

00:05:10.276 --> 00:05:11.877
Okay, yeah, they're naked
and they're wrestling

00:05:11.877 --> 00:05:13.546
and they're having sex
and blah, blah, blah."

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:15.782
And then I thought,
"Oh, God, that's me."

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:18.084
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.084 --> 00:05:20.253
Now I go and I sit
and I watch it

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:22.021
on a movie screen
with other people.

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:23.789
Last night we had a premiere in
New York.

00:05:23.789 --> 00:05:26.058
My half-brother had to sit
through that.

00:05:26.058 --> 00:05:28.394
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:30.463
-Well, you put the work in
and it paid off.

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:31.864
-Thank you.

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:33.599
-First of all, it's always
a delight to have you here.

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:34.933
-I love you.
-But especially for this.

00:05:34.933 --> 00:05:36.168
It is such a wonderful film.
-Thank you.

00:05:36.168 --> 00:05:38.704
-Congratulations.
Everybody go see "Bros."

00:05:38.704 --> 00:05:39.871
-Go see "Bros"!

00:05:39.871 --> 00:05:41.641
-It's in theaters
September 30th.

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:43.409
We'll be right back
with Beth Ditto.

